  "supportingPhenomena": "• A ladder leaning against a wall is safest at a particular angle; changing the angle changes how high the ladder reaches although its length stays the same.\n• The shadow of a tree or flagpole at a given time of day is longer or shorter in a fixed proportion to its height, however tall the object.\n• A pilot descending into Jomo Kenyatta International Airport follows a steady angle of descent that links height to horizontal distance.\n• The scientific calculator gives sin 30° = 0.5 and cos 60° = 0.5, which seems like more than a coincidence.",
