        "teacherMoves": "Say: \"On our model, we had an angle and a missing length. What goes in the middle that connects them?\" WAIT TIME of 15 seconds. Cold-call 3 learners to suggest wording, and agree a class version. Ask: \"What do we still not know in the model?\" Expect: how to get the ratio for an angle quickly, and how to turn the ratio into a length. Write these as 'next steps'. Finish with: \"Wanjiru's multiplier 0.70 comes from her 35 degree angle. Next lesson we will check that number using tables and calculators.\" Collect one exit slip: 'Write the definition of tan theta and say which two sides it uses.'",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Cumulative model revision: learners update a shared model with new evidence, keeping a record of what is explained so far and what is still unknown. This makes the middle step of the model, the ratio, explicit.",
