      "purposeInStoryline": "Lesson 2 showed that for a 35 degree angle the ratios are constant (opp/adj = 0.70) and defined sin, cos and tan. Wanjiru Kamau cannot draw triangles on site, so she needs the ratio from a reliable source. This lesson shows that tables and calculators give the same ratios we measured, so the multiplier 0.7002 for 35 degrees can be trusted. It also builds the class table of values (10 to 80 degrees) that Lesson 4 will use to compare complementary angles.",
      "safetyNotes": "No specific hazards. Remind learners to handle calculators and geometry sets carefully and not to leave pencils and compasses on the floor."
