        "teacherMoves": "Say: \"Wanjiru stands in Nairobi with no ruler and no paper. Yet she uses 0.7002 for 35 degrees. Where could that number come from? Write your prediction and your reason.\" Give WAIT TIME of 15 seconds before anyone writes, then 2 minutes for writing. Cold-call 3 learners: \"What do you expect tan 35 to be and why?\" Do not confirm or correct. Record predictions on the board under 'Predicted value of tan 35' with a tally. Ask: \"Will the table match our drawn triangles exactly, nearly, or not at all?\" Take a show of hands.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Predict-Share-Revisit: committing to a prediction with a reason makes learners notice later whether the evidence supports their idea, which focuses attention on comparing measured and tabulated values.",
