        "teacherMoves": "Say: \"Last lesson our model said that the angle fixes the ratio. What do we add today?\" WAIT TIME of 10 seconds. Cold-call 2 learners to suggest additions and ask 1 learner to explain the revision in their own words. Add the new box to the poster and ask: \"Which ratio does Wanjiru use, and why that one?\" (tan 35, because she knows the adjacent side of 100 m and wants the opposite side). Ask learners to complete the exit ticket: 'Write sin 35, cos 35 and tan 35 to 4 d.p., and name one reason a measured ratio may differ from the table value.' Collect and sample.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Cumulative model revision: adding a new component to the shared model each lesson shows how evidence builds a full explanation of the phenomenon.",
