    "teacherReflection": "1. Did every group get 0.5736, 0.8192 and 0.7002 for 35 degrees from both tables and calculator? Which groups had the calculator in the wrong mode, and how did they discover it?\n2. How well did learners explain the difference between measured and tabulated ratios as measurement error rather than a different angle?\n3. Which learners struggled to read the tables, and what support (row guides, partner checks) helped?\n4. What questions did learners raise about patterns in the table, and how will you use them in Lessons 4 and 5?\n5. Does the revised model help learners see how Wanjiru's 0.7002 comes from the angle alone?",
