        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Wanjiru's triangle has a right angle and a 35° angle. What is the third angle? Show me on your whiteboards.' Then ask: 'Do you think sin 35° and any ratio of 55° could be related? Write your prediction and one reason.' WAIT TIME: 15 seconds of silent thinking before partner talk. Cold-call 4 learners to share predictions, and record all of them on the board without judging, including 'no relation'.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Predict-and-record (commit before evidence): writing a prediction first gives learners a stake in the evidence, and unjudged predictions on the board can later be tested and revised.",
