    "teacherReflection": "1. Did learners find 90° − θ correctly and use it in their relationship, or did they just match equal numbers? What evidence did you see?\n2. Which groups gave a reason based on the triangle (opposite and adjacent swap), and which relied only on the table? How will you support the second kind in Lesson 5?\n3. How many calculators were in RAD mode, and how did you catch it? What will you do next time?\n4. Which DQB questions came from learners, and did anyone ask about tan? How will you use them in Lesson 5?\n5. Did the 45°/45° pair prompt useful discussion? What would you change about the table or the timing?",
