        "teacherMoves": "Say: \"Write one thing we can now answer and one new question on separate notes.\" Give 15 seconds of silent WAIT TIME before writing. Cold-call 3 learners to read a note aloud and place it; ask the class: \"Does this question need an instrument, a table or a triangle?\" Point out that Lesson 7 will use a clinometer to measure real angles and that tables and calculators give other angles like 35°. Move answered questions to the answered side and keep new ones visible.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Question tracking on the DQB: sorting questions into answered and unanswered shows learners how their understanding grows and creates a purpose for the next lesson on the clinometer, angle of elevation and angle of depression.",
