        "teacherMoves": "Say: \"Add what today's triangles tell us to our model. Where does the angle come in, where do the ratios come in?\" Give 15 seconds of WAIT TIME, then let groups work for 4 minutes. Cold-call 2 groups to explain their addition and ask: \"How would this change if the ladder were at 30° instead of 60°?\" (expected: height 4.0 x 0.5000 = 2.0 m). Finish by asking each learner to complete an exit ticket: 'Write the exact values of sin, cos and tan of 45° and say which triangle they came from.'",
