        "learnerExperience": "Groups revise the class model poster 'angle -> ratio of sides -> unknown length'. They add: 'measure angle of elevation with a clinometer', 'measure horizontal distance on the ground', 'unknown height above eye = distance x tan angle', and 'add eye height'. They add a small drawing of angle of depression linked to elevation by alternate angles. (4 minutes)",
        "teacherMoves": "Say: \"What new step have we added to the model today? Where does eye height fit in? Where would Wanjiru's 35 degrees and 100 m go?\" Give 10 to 15 seconds WAIT TIME. Cold-call 2 groups to place cards on the poster. Ask: \"What is still missing from our explanation of why the same angle works for a small flagpole triangle and a big building triangle?\" Point out that Lesson 8 will answer this fully.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Cumulative model revision: learners add to a shared visual model each lesson, linking evidence to the explanation of the phenomenon and showing the chain from angle to ratio to length.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Look for model additions that connect the clinometer reading to the tan ratio and then to height. Check whether learners include eye height and show the correct place for the angle and the distance. Listen for correct use of 'ratio'. Note gaps for Lesson 8."
